questions.text:
The department of public health has approached you to assist in representing some concepts with semantic graph. The narrative is as follows: there are 4 main concepts – Disease, Drug, Gene, and Compound. Compound could interact with compound. Compound includes pharmacologic class and interacts with food. Drug causes side-effects and are used to treat disease. Disease have types and symptoms. It also has target in gene. Gene is part-of pathway, biological process, molecular function, and component. Gene interacts with compound, it is expressedby anatomy, associatedwith disease while disease localizes anatomy and its treatedby compound. Compound also belongsTo ATC class and compound causes side effects.

Suppose we can isolate the following:
Disease {Types, Symptoms}
Drug
Gene {Anatomy, Pathway, Biological process, Molecular function, Component}
Compound {ATC class, Pharmacologic class, Food, Side effect}

i. Employ the information above to present a semantic graph (10 marks)
ii. Draw out 5 functional complete sentences with meaning from the graph (5 marks)
